{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":1086,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ezek.25","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Ezekiel","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Ezekiel 25","reference":"Ezekiel 25","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"A prophesy against the Ammonites, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-7.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"The Moabites, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"8-11.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"The Edomites, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"12-14.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"And the Philistines, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":8,"text":"15- 17.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":9,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":10,"text":"Aha - When thou shouldest have pitied, thou didst proudly insult over my people.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":11,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":12,"text":"The men of the east - The Arabians, associates of Nebuchadnezzar, who recompensed their service, with giving them this country when it was conquered, as it was five years after the desolation of Jerusalem.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":13,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":14,"text":"Rabbah - The royal city, called since Philadelphia from the king of Egypt who built it.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":15,"text":"The Ammonites - The land they dwelt in.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":16,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":17,"text":"Know - Thus God will bring those that were strangers to him into an acquaintance with him, and it will be a blessed effect of their calamities.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":18,"text":"How much better is it, to be poor and know God, than to be rich, and ignorant of him?","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":19,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":20,"text":"Seir - The seed of Esau, the Edomites.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":21,"text":"Seir was the mountain where they first planted themselves.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":22,"text":"Is like - Are no more a select people than others.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":23,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":24,"text":"The side - That part of his country which was best fortified.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":25,"text":"Bethjeshimoth - An ancient city; it was a fortress toward the desert, which watched lest any should make an inroad on the country.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":26,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":27,"text":"With the Ammonites - As I have given Ammon, so I will with them give Moab to the Chaldeans, who will give it to the Arabians.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":28,"text":"13.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":29,"text":"Teman - A country in the southern coast of Edom.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":30,"text":"Dedan - Adjoining to Edom.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":31,"text":"15.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":32,"text":"It - Israel.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":33,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":34,"text":"The Cherethim - The bowmen, the strength of Philistia.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":35,"text":"The remnant - Who had escaped the sword of Samuel, David, Hezekiah, and of Psammetichus king of Egypt.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":25}}